{# An account's face, at whatever size the caller sets `--yw-avatar-size` to.

   One partial for both cases -- a picture and a pair of initials -- because a caller
   drawing "who this is" does not want to know which of the two it got, and because the
   round frame, the size and the way it sits on a line have to be identical either way or
   the navbar moves when someone uploads a photo.

   The two colours are inline because they are data, not design: they are computed from the
   account's name (AvatarService), so there is no stylesheet that could know them. #}
{# Takes `avatar` (a YesWiki\Identity\Entity\Avatar) and an optional `class`. #}
<span class="yw-avatar{{ class|default('') ? ' ' ~ class }}"
      {% if not avatar.hasImage %}style="--yw-avatar-bg: {{ avatar.background }}; --yw-avatar-fg: {{ avatar.foreground }};"{% endif %}
      aria-hidden="true">
  {%- if avatar.hasImage -%}
    <img class="yw-avatar__image" src="{{ avatar.imageUrl }}" alt="" loading="lazy" />
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="yw-avatar__initials">{{ avatar.initials }}</span>
  {%- endif -%}
</span>
